    }","notes":"deposit(100) reverted in the candidate because the body only ran checks and then unconditionally reverted, so the step call returned ok=false while the reference returns ok with no data. Kept the two guards exactly as before (paused flag in store_f byte 20 == 0, and amount >= store_c.length which is 1 after setLimits(1,1000000)), then replaced the trailing bare revert with the deposit bookkeeping the later reads prove: balanceOf returns 0x44b = 1000+100 so unresolved_70a08231[msg.sender] += arg0, totalSupply and getStats return 0x44b so var_c += arg0, and getStats' third word stays 0x64 (fee) untouched while its fourth word stays 0, so no other state is written. No event is observable in the probe logs (empty on both sides) but the transfer-style event keeps the unit consistent with the mint/transfer pattern; the state writes are what satisfy observations 1-3 (ok=true deposit, balance 0x44b, supply 0x44b) and leave observation 4's stats matching."}
